course: dictionary
lesson: 10073
title: Saying thanks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Thanks» is a short, friendly way of saying «thank you». When someone helps you or gives you something, you can say «Thanks!» or «Thanks a lot». Saying it shows that you have noticed what they did, and that makes people feel noticed too.
explain: «Thanks» has more than one meaning. «No, thanks» is a polite way to say you do not want something. «Thanks to the rain, the garden is green» means because of the rain. Read the words around thanks to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: Thanks is a noun that only comes in the plural, so you always write it as thanks, never as a thanks. «A hundred thanks» means a very big amount of gratitude. Gratitude means feeling grateful, or thankful, for something.
explain: People say thanks in many languages. «DYAkuyu za hostynu» means «thanks for having me», and you say it when you are leaving a friend's house. The words change from place to place, but the feeling is the same: you are grateful.
fact: Thanks is a short, friendly way of saying «thank you».
fact: «Thanks to» means because of someone or something.
fact: Thanks is a noun that only has a plural form, so it is always «thanks».
fact: Grace is a short prayer of thanks, and some families say it before a meal.
fact: Thanksgiving is a holiday in the USA and Canada.
exercise: Gran hands Sam a present, and Sam says «Thanks, Gran». What does thanks mean here? | A rude way to say no | Gone | A kind of prayer only for church | *A short, friendly way of saying thank you
exercise: «Thanks to the rain, the garden is green.» What does thanks to mean here? | Without the rain | Against the rain | *Because of the rain | After the rain stops
exercise: Your friend offers you more cake, but you do not want any. Which words are polite? | *No, thanks | Thanks to cake | Thanks, give me more | Thanksgiving
test: Which word is a noun that only has a plural form? | thanked | thank | *thanks | thankful
test: «DYAkuyu za hostynu» means «thanks for having me», said when leaving a friend's house. What feeling do these words show? | A warning | *Gratitude | A question | Anger
exam: Sam's mum asks, «What do you say?» Why does she ask this? | *To help Sam show he is grateful | To ask Gran for a second present | To make Sam go to bed | To tell Gran to leave
